   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi folks,</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve just updated my version of R to 4.3 and am now having problems with running various dartR functions. <br></div><div><br></div><div>For instance when I try to run gl.report.secondaries(gl) I get the following:</div><div>The column &#39;TrimmedSequence&#39; was not found in loc.metrics<br> Mean tag length assumed to be 69</div><div>Error in p1/p2 : non-numeric argument to binary operator</div><div><br></div><div>My current dataset has &quot;TrimmedSequenceRef&quot; and &quot;TrimmedSequenceSnp&quot; columns, but if I delete the second column and rename the first to &quot;TrimmedSequence&quot; before reading the file in, I still get the warning and the error.</div><div><br></div><div>I did not previously have this problem with this data set. I&#39;m also now getting the same error for various other dartR functions, even with the test data sets. I&#39;ve tried this with both the current CRAN version of dartR (v2.7.2) and with the developmental version (v2.9.4).</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div><div>Peter<br></div><div><br></div><br></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Fri, 14 Apr 2023 at 14:09, Jose Luis Mijangos &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">luis.m...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
